50808.sol:
By Malus Law, we have<br>\[
I=I_{0} \cos $\theta$\]<br>Given, intensity of light from second polariser is half of that from the first polariser, so<br>\[
$\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow\frac{I_{0}}{2}=I_{0} \cos ^{2} \theta\\
\Rightarrow \cos ^{2} \theta=\frac{1}{2}\\
\Rightarrow \cos \theta=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\\
\Rightarrow \theta=\cos ^{-1} \left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)\\
\Rightarrow \theta=45^{{}^{\circ}}
\end{array}
\]<br>Therefore, angle between the pass axes of polarisers is \( 45^{{}^{\circ}} \).$

